        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix(discord): log warnings instead of silently swallowing component interaction errors",
        "body": "## What Problem This Solves\n\n`extensions/discord/src/monitor/agent-components-reply.ts` and `extensions/discord/src/monitor/exec-approvals.ts` use empty `catch {}` blocks to silently swallow errors from Discord interaction replies. When these replies fail (expired interaction, network issue, permission error), there is zero diagnostic output — making debugging impossible.\n\n## Changes\n\n- `agent-components-reply.ts`: `catch {}` → `catch (err) { console.warn(\"discord component reply failed\", ...) }`\n- `exec-approvals.ts`: 4 sites → `catch (err) { console.warn(\"discord exec approval ... failed\", ...) }`\n- `agent-components-reply.test.ts`: 2 vitest tests (success no-warn, failure → warn logged)\n- `exec-approvals.test.ts`: 4 vitest diagnostic tests covering all catch paths (reply, unauthorized reply, acknowledge, followUp failures)\n\nLabel: bugfix | merge-risk: 🟢 minimal | AI-assisted\n\n## Evidence\n\n### Vitest — all 7 new diagnostic tests\n\n```\npnpm exec vitest run extensions/discord/src/monitor/agent-components-reply.test.ts\n\n ✓ replySilently > calls interaction.reply and does not warn on success\n ✓ replySilently > logs console.warn when interaction.reply throws\n\npnpm exec vitest run extensions/discord/src/monitor/exec-approvals.test.ts\n\n ✓ ExecApprovalButton diagnostic logging > logs warn when reply throws\n ✓ ExecApprovalButton diagnostic logging > logs warn when unauthorized reply throws\n ✓ ExecApprovalButton diagnostic logging > logs warn when acknowledge throws\n ✓ ExecApprovalButton diagnostic logging > logs warn when followUp throws\n ... (all 12 existing exec-approval tests pass)\n```\n\n### Call chain (production)\n\nDiscord gateway → component interaction → `replySilently()` / `ExecApprovalButton.run()` → Discord API HTTP reply → if throws → `console.warn(...)` (was silent catch {})\n\n### Negative control (L3)\n\nReverting `catch (err) { console.warn(...) }` to `catch {}` causes the new tests to fail — `warnSpy` is never called, confirming the fix is real.",
